=== unsized ===
\e[?2026h\e[?25l\e]133;A\e\\\e[48;2;52;53;65m\e[0m\r
\e[48;2;52;53;65m what does the accented file say? 🖊\e[0m\r
\e[48;2;52;53;65m\e[0m\r
\e[3m\e[38;2;150;152;150mReading the file with the combining marks in its name.\e[0m\e[0m\r
\r
The name is written \e[38;2;192;128;80mcafé\e[0m rather than \e[38;2;192;128;80mcafé\e[0m, so the accent is a mark of its own.\r
\r
A family 👨‍👩‍👧 is one glyph joined from several, and a heart ❤️ asks to be drawn in colour.\r
\r
Combining marks pile up too: á̂̃̄ is one letter under four of them.\r
\r
A spacing mark is not a combining one: Thai \e[38;2;192;128;80mกำ\e[0m and Devanagari \e[38;2;192;128;80mकि\e[0m are two characters apiece, and each takes the one cell its base took.\r
\r
A keycap 1️⃣ asks for two, where a bare 1⃣ keeps the one its digit had.\r
\r
